,"site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-08T21:55:17Z","updated_at":"2025-07-08T21:55:17Z","body":"+1. I was having a very productive coding session with 2.5 Pro until suddenly, I was downgraded to Flash without even being presented an option to say \"no.\" This was a horrible user experience as Flash either completely ignored or simply could not understand the the context and instructions I had spent hours carefully crafting. Any attempt to guide it back on track just resulted in more script-kiddie behavior.\n\nIf Google can't handle the demand that the pro model is placing on their systems, that's fine. But at least let me switch back to manual coding or another agent rather than just ruining the useful work the Pro model produced since my last commit!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3050399169/reactions","total_count":7,"+1":7,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3084291453","html_url":"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208#issuecomment-3084291453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208","id":3084291453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOObWEYM631o19","user":{"login":"snowliondev","id":1651391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTEzOTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1651391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev","html_url":"https://github.com/snowliondev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/snowliondev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-17T14:26:23Z","updated_at":"2025-07-17T14:27:35Z","body":"It's too dangerous to put Gemini in auto-accept changes when flash fallback is even a possibility. It went about entirely reversing a whole bunch of features. The fact that it can just sneak in asking, and I'm sure even one time it was telling me it was on Pro, but behaving exactly like it was on Flash. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3084291453/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3352820163","html_url":"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208#issuecomment-3352820163","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208","id":3352820163,"node_id":"IC_kwDOObWEYM7H1_nD","user":{"login":"dikelps","id":100877195,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgNDiw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100877195?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps","html_url":"https://github.com/dikelps","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dikelps/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-30T15:47:38Z","updated_at":"2025-09-30T15:47:38Z","body":"I cannot trust flash in any capacity with the edit. I'd rather write by hand than to review anything flash comes up with. Please add this simple feature to completely disable the flash models. In a recent incident during the downtime of pro models the CLI did not display it was using flash on the right bottom but it was, this behavior was immediately caught because the quality difference is simply massive, but I'd rather not have to worry about those hidden behavior. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3352820163/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":4,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3390185245","html_url":"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208#issuecomment-3390185245","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208","id":3390185245,"node_id":"IC_kwDOObWEYM7KEh8d","user":{"login":"RetroInsanity","id":58904008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4OTA0MDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58904008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity","html_url":"https://github.com/RetroInsanity","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RetroInsanity/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-10T13:39:12Z","updated_at":"2025-10-10T13:39:12Z","body":"Yeah, I can literally not believe this is STILL going on several months later!  \"Backlog - a good idea but not currently a priority\" pretty much says it all. Constant interruption of the workflow to switch models, while not even giving the user the option to wait renders every other fix the developers could do on CLI pretty much pointless for everyone except paid API users. I get that you want to basically slay the free users (a-la Spotify) and make it completely unviable to use the free tier. But meanwhile I have a paid Google Workspace Business Plus account which seems to give me a decent amount of AI usage on Web with Gemini 2.5 PRO model, but I can't even use that for CLI without incurring extra billing. I think what we are really asking for is fairness and transparency.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3390185245/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/comments/3451316404","html_url":"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208#issuecomment-3451316404","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google-gemini/gemini-cli/issues/2208","id":3451316404,"node_id":"IC_kwDOObWEYM7Ntui0","user":{"login":"Exadra37","id":1745456,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDU0NTY=","avatar_url":"https://